{"answer": "C", "estimate": 391, "mechanism": "C", "confidence": 95, "reasoning": "In PHP 8, each array is a Zend HashTable. The outer array stores 1M buckets (32 bytes each). Each inner array is a separate allocation containing a header (~64 bytes) and a minimum of 8 buckets (8 * 32 = 256 bytes), totaling ~320 bytes. Adding outer bucket costs and ZMM allocator overhead leads to ~410 bytes per pair."}
