```json
{"answer": "B", "estimate": 18, "mechanism": "C", "confidence": 90, "reasoning": "In Go 1.24, Swiss tables store keys and values in aligned slots. map[int64]struct{} has a slot size of 8 bytes (key only), while map[int64]bool has a slot size of 16 bytes (key+bool, padded for alignment). With 1M entries and a ~87.5% load factor, the map grows to 2^21 slots, making set ~18MB and flags ~34MB."}
